-- title:
--   Reindexing predictions along equivalent candidate labels
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. Let $e:I\to J$ be a bijection of finite candidate label sets that preserves parents.
--
--   1. **Pulled coefficients.** $\theta\mapsto\theta\circ e$ maps the coefficient set for $J$ onto the one for $I$, preserving every group mass:
--   $$
--   \sum_i\theta^p_{e(i)}=\sum_j\theta^p_j .
--   $$
--   2. **Invariance.** Residual inputs, evaluated predictions and the chosen weak limits are unchanged under this reindexing. Hence the detector sets built from a recorded history agree with those built from the final ledger.
